  "question": {
    "text": "Two monochromatic light beams of intensity 16 and 9 units are interfering. The ratio of intensities of bright and dark parts of the resultant pattern is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "BPjGK",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{16}{9}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "OYerD",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{4}{3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "MLIlH",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{7}{1}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Q71Tn",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{49}{1}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Intensity $\\propto(\\text { amplitude })^2$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{I_1}{I_2}=\\frac{16}{9}=\\frac{a_1^2}{a_2^2} \\\\\n&\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{a}_1=4 ; \\mathrm{a}_2=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nTherefore the ratio of intensities of bright and dark parts\n$$\n\\frac{I_{\\text {Bright }}}{I_{\\text {Dark }}}=\\frac{\\left(a_1+a_2\\right)^2}{\\left(a_1-a_2\\right)^2}=\\frac{(4+3)^2}{(4-3)^2}=\\frac{49}{1}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
